course: dictionary
lesson: 223
title: What is an alkali?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An alkali is a chemical that is the opposite of an acid. It can cancel out an acid, so the two often react when they meet.
explain: «Baking soda is a mild alkali, the opposite of an acid.» Alkalis dissolve in water and make a solution with a pH above 7 on the pH scale.
explain: Scientists test for alkalis with indicators. «Litmus paper turns red in acid and blue in alkali», so a blue colour tells you an alkali is there.
explain: Be careful: «Strong alkalis, like some oven cleaners, can burn skin and eyes.» Always wear goggles and gloves when you handle cleaning products.
fact: An alkali is a chemical that is the opposite of an acid.
fact: An alkali can cancel out an acid.
fact: Alkalis dissolve in water and give a pH above 7.
fact: The pH scale runs from 0 to 14: below 7 is acid, 7 is neutral, and above 7 is alkali.
fact: Alkalis are found in soap, toothpaste, baking soda and indigestion tablets.
exercise: «Baking soda is a mild alkali, the opposite of an acid.» What is an alkali the opposite of? | Salt | Water | *An acid | Light
exercise: «Litmus paper turns red in acid and blue in alkali.» What colour does litmus paper turn in an alkali? | Red | *Blue | Green | Yellow
exercise: On the pH scale, which number shows an alkali? | 3 | 7 | 0 | *10
test: «The acid in the vinegar and the alkali in the soda react and make a new gas, which bubbles out.» What does the alkali do to the acid? | Turns it into water only | *Reacts with it and makes a new gas | Makes it turn red | Makes it cool down
test: Red cabbage juice is blue-green with a mild alkali like baking soda. What colour is it with an acid? | Yellow | *Pink-red | Blue-green | Purple
exam: Which statement about alkalis is true? | Alkalis are acids that have been heated | Alkalis have a pH below 7 | Alkalis always make your skin feel better | *Strong alkalis, like some oven cleaners, can burn skin and eyes
